{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15982-making-geister-more-important-wraithfying-geist","id":15982,"title":"Making Geister more important (Wraithfying Geist)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-22T02:00:49-08:00","id":15982,"title":"Making Geister more important (Wraithfying Geist)","content":"Geister are creatures somewhere between ghosts and gods, yes? They're also intrinsically metaphysically removed from the world of the living - unlike ghosts, they have no way to exist in the Flesh or even in Twilight.<br /> <br /> That's where mortals come in.<br /> <br /> Both a dead mortal and a Geist have much to gain from the Bargain - the mortal gets a second chance at life. The Geist gets to exist in the mortal world at all.<br /> <br /> The Bargain isn't a singular event, but a constant process. Geister have their own agendas, goals and things they need to achieve in the mortal world. Sometimes these goals even overlap with those of the mortal. Occasionally the Geist can convince the mortal to do things for him. Other times, both mortal and Geist struggle over command of the body both share.<br /> <br /> The Geist is the source of power keeping the fused identity of the Sin-Eater alive. If the mortal is weak, it can offer additional strength and protection. There's always a price, though, and it's the constant negotiation between human and Geist that defines the Sin-Eater condition.<br /> <br /> This is my attempt to bring a little Wraith into the Geist game. The Geist is the little voice in the Sin-Eater's head that tells him to do very bad things. Being part gods, Geister desire for things to happen that metaphysically resonate with their being. Being part ghosts, the things they need to happen are usually focused on negative things. A Geist that was created during an act of treason wants to further the cause of treason in the world. Some Geister just want to stab people in the eyes. Others might have cults of death that they care about, that they would see protected and taken care of.<br /> <br /> In this particular setting hack for Geist: the Sin-Eaters, the Geist takes on an active role in the game, similar to the Shadow in Wraith. Geister are capable of being in constant communion with their hosts, taunting them, offering them advice and trying to make deals.<br /> <br /> So how does it work?<br /> (I'm deliberately not using system terms here, because I don't use Storytelling to run Geist.)<br /> <br /> The Sin-Eater regains energy by completing tasks that the Geist wants him to do. These are always things that are thematically appropriate for gods of death, and that cause trouble (story hooks) in the long or short term - hurting people, causing mayhem, etc.<br /> <br /> The Sin-Eater also regains energy in exchange for Shadow points. Shadow points represent the influence the Geist has over the human. Accrue enough Shadow points and the Geist can try to take over the body for a time, enabling him to do the things he wants.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T06:56:28-08:00","id":16089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15982-making-geister-more-important-wraithfying-geist#post15982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geister are creatures somewhere between ghosts and gods, yes? They're also intrinsically metaphysically removed from the world of the living - unlike ghosts, they have no way to exist in the Flesh or even in Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Unfettered geister can freely leave the Underworld without having to worry about staying near anchors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Bargain isn't a singular event, but a constant process. Geister have their own agendas, goals and things they need to achieve in the mortal world. Sometimes these goals even overlap with those of the mortal. Occasionally the Geist can convince the mortal to do things for him. Other times, both mortal and Geist struggle over command of the body both share. </div> </div> </div>This is a notion I've been somewhat enamored of <a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=posts&amp;m=1516462#post1516462\" target=\"_blank\">for a while</a> and I'd certainly like to see more of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thoughts? </div> </div> </div>I feel as though some of this amounts to mechanizing the &quot;geister as advocates for particular forms of death&quot; aspect of the game, but I also feel that making this result in more control from the geist rather than a greater synthesis between host and tenant is kind of a wrongheaded direction to take it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T06:58:38-08:00","id":16091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15982-making-geister-more-important-wraithfying-geist?p=16089#post16089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though some of this amounts to mechanizing the &quot;geister as advocates for particular forms of death&quot; aspect of the game, but I also feel that making this result in more control from the geist rather than a greater synthesis between host and tenant is kind of a wrongheaded direction to take it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Synthesis explicitly isn't what I'm going for, because I like there to be a conflict between the mortal and the Geist on some level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T06:59:53-08:00","id":16092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15982-making-geister-more-important-wraithfying-geist?p=16089#post16089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. Unfettered geister can freely leave the Underworld without having to worry about staying near anchors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in this setting hack, they can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T07:04:38-08:00","id":16095,"title":"","content":"This is a cornerstone of my work in progress massive revision of Geist to the GMC rules. However I'm putting in a major focus on the Geist's human past rather than the god angle and rather than offering power in a dark bargain it's more a straight up battle for control. I'm also tying it into Krewes in special ways, making it the backbone of Thresholds and all sorts of coolness <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Some Geists and Sin-Eaters just really get on, so Geist's giving freebies was out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T07:06:12-08:00","id":16096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15982-making-geister-more-important-wraithfying-geist?p=16092#post16092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not in this setting hack, they can't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could've been clearer. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T07:28:38-08:00","id":16101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15982-making-geister-more-important-wraithfying-geist?p=16096#post16096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could've been clearer. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>My mistake, sorry <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T07:33:04-08:00","id":16102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15982-making-geister-more-important-wraithfying-geist?p=16095#post16095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a cornerstone of my work in progress massive revision of Geist to the GMC rules. However I'm putting in a major focus on the Geist's human past rather than the god angle and rather than offering power in a dark bargain it's more a straight up battle for control. I'm also tying it into Krewes in special ways, making it the backbone of Thresholds and all sorts of coolness <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Some Geists and Sin-Eaters just really get on, so Geist's giving freebies was out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it when relations are a bit more complicated rather than a straight up battle for control. It can be that, sometimes, yes - there should absolutely be room for conflict between the Geist and the human, but, especially as degeneration settles in, there should also be a place for common ground between the Geist and the human.<br /> <br /> Definitely no freebies, though.<br /> <br /> And I enjoy emphasising the god angle of the Geister. I kind of like the idea of people being reanimated/sharing a common body with an actual real god of death. Gives the game more of a mythological touch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T08:40:03-08:00","id":16117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15982-making-geister-more-important-wraithfying-geist?p=16102#post16102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like it when relations are a bit more complicated rather than a straight up battle for control. It can be that, sometimes, yes - there should absolutely be room for conflict between the Geist and the human, but, especially as degeneration settles in, there should also be a place for common ground between the Geist and the human.<br /> <br /> Definitely no freebies, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading my post again I phrased it really really badly (I'm kinda asleep at the moment...)<br /> <br /> The core mechanical system is a battle for control, but that's the linchpin for other systems that basically provide elaborate alternatives to needing to fight (i.e. The possibility of fighting your Geist provides importance to the mechanics based around avoiding fights).<br /> <br /> If the PC fulfils her Geist's desires or uncovers/resolves aspects of the past you earn points that can be spent to avoid any conflicts of wills. If there is common ground and you don't ask your Geist for too much power (I'm making Geists control Manifestations, but Ceremonies have a major power boost) you could probably go the entire game without having to roll for a conflict.<br /> <br /> On the other hand a 0 Synergy character dedicated to keeping his evil Geist imprisoned in his soul is also a valid concept thanks to the design of the system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15982-making-geister-more-important-wraithfying-geist?p=16102#post16102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I enjoy emphasising the god angle of the Geister. I kind of like the idea of people being reanimated/sharing a common body with an actual real god of death. Gives the game more of a mythological touch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I think you'll like what I'm doing with Krewes then. Mythologies, Metaphysics and all that jazz now have mechanical effects.<br /> <br /> The core Geist systems are based on it's personal desires (the Geist's Vice-equivalent) and it's human past (Virtue-equivalent) but the Krewe myths and such directly plug into the same systems giving an additional Virtue or Vice equivalent based on playing to your Geist's mythological role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T10:58:01-08:00","id":16181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15982-making-geister-more-important-wraithfying-geist#post15982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is my attempt to bring a little Wraith into the Geist game.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why? Why would you ever want to do this? I certainly want to express that I respect you as a player. However, Wraith: The Oblivion was one of the most horrible RPG's that White Wolf ever made...ever. Geist, and the way it works now is a really great system that has become one of my favorite to Storytell in. Bringing more &quot;Wraith&quot; into &quot;Geist&quot; is like saying, &quot;I sure wish there was more Spam in my pumpkin pie! Wouldnt it be great?&quot; No, sir, it would not.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Nothing is foolproof for a sufficiently talented fool.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/981-bigwhitt","name":"bigwhitt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T11:07:49-08:00","id":16189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bigwhitt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15982-making-geister-more-important-wraithfying-geist?p=16181#post16181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why? Why would you ever want to do this? I certainly want to express that I respect you as a player. However, Wraith: The Oblivion was one of the most horrible RPG's that White Wolf ever made...ever. Geist, and the way it works now is a really great system that has become one of my favorite to Storytell in. Bringing more &quot;Wraith&quot; into &quot;Geist&quot; is like saying, &quot;I sure wish there was more Spam in my pumpkin pie! Wouldnt it be great?&quot; No, sir, it would not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously, my tastes as a player and storyteller are different from yours in that regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T11:22:28-08:00","id":16195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15982-making-geister-more-important-wraithfying-geist#post15982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being part gods, Geister desire for things to happen that metaphysically resonate with their being.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gods? Do you mean spirit? Or something else? <br /> I seriously need to reread this book, I missed this entire Horsemen connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T12:34:51-08:00","id":16233,"title":"","content":"*happens by, sipping a cooling tot of tea*<br /> <br /> Hmph. Oh I see....*picking up the thread and perusing it quietly: or not so:* Oh interesting....and this....oh my....and that?.....I see.<br /> <br /> *places it nicely back where he found it, smoothing out a few crinkles n'wrinkles; then shrugs, a soft smirk of mirth forming.*<br /> <br /> Feasible. Though many of the things you've written here, are already fundamentals of the game as it exists. (Though clearly freshened, and given a nice coat of primer by your words herein.) I liken it to Bengal Tiger; where I am an Earl Grey fan, personally. <br /> <br /> I have but, two suggestions: regarding the nature of how your Geists would be Shadows/Wraiths in this particular murder-scene:<br /> <br /> 1. If you are playing with either Very experienced players who like things extra challenging, or Newbies who have never played the game, perhaps keeping the Geists a secret primarily could be an interesting tryst to explore. Perhaps the character(s) die, and then return with no memory of what happens. (Story-wise, perhaps they wake up in the hospital, or they wake up lying on the ground where they had been struck down from this poor, poor, mortal coil.) They continue the game as a Mortal game, but have the occasional &quot;Haunting&quot; experience; and a distant voice (the Geist, getting itself situated, perhaps; like an unfamiliar bottom in a new, comfy chair!) that whispers secrets about Death and the power it can have in and over Life. Eventually the Geist may reveal itself, and the powers it can perform for the characters become more manual, and under their own control. (Rather than having to &quot;Ask the Dark Voice to do it for them.&quot;) At some hair-raising point, they realize that a few of the things the voice has been asking them to do, (I would personally lead up from small things, until they're in over their head: maybe even do the old Shadow thing where the Geist occasionally takes control during certain circumstances; or at special times of day/night.) doesn't really sit right with them. Lay about long-story-arcs that compel them to -of course- go for the easy power grabs, but then slowly tighten the noose, and make them realize when it's (fairly, now.) too late that they have Bargained into something truly, truly frightening.<br /> <br /> 2. Two....now...what was two.....*stares off into the open air a moment, eventually settling his gaze quietly on the back of Satchel's head, and beginning to vaguely wonder this or that*....Hmph, it had something to do with tea, I'm sure.....<br /> <br /> *wanders off in thought*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1219-shake","name":"Shake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T00:37:05-08:00","id":16509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15982-making-geister-more-important-wraithfying-geist?p=16195#post16195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gods? Do you mean spirit? Or something else?<br /> I seriously need to reread this book, I missed this entire Horsemen connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Geister have always been presented as something somewhere between ghosts and gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T00:40:29-08:00","id":16510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bb