casional &quot;Haunting&quot; experience; and a distant voice (the Geist, getting itself situated, perhaps; like an unfamiliar bottom in a new, comfy chair!) that whispers secrets about Death and the power it can have in and over Life. Eventually the Geist may reveal itself, and the powers it can perform for the characters become more manual, and under their own control. (Rather than having to &quot;Ask the Dark Voice to do it for them.&quot;) At some hair-raising point, they realize that a few of the things the voice has been asking them to do, (I would personally lead up from small things, until they're in over their head: maybe even do the old Shadow thing where the Geist occasionally takes control during certain circumstances; or at special times of day/night.) doesn't really sit right with them. Lay about long-story-arcs that compel them to -of course- go for the easy power grabs, but then slowly tighten the noose, and make them realize when it's (fairly, now.) too late that they have Bargained into something truly, truly frightening.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a nice idea. Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T13:24:16-08:00","id":16759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15982-making-geister-more-important-wraithfying-geist#post15982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I'm deliberately not using system terms here, because I don't use Storytelling to run Geist.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious, even though this is a little bit off topic: What system DO you use to run Geist?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>ST/DM for <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCfFy7kNgMvxIR1qdzT8PzEg\" target=\"_blank\">Dice Alternatives</a><br /> Playing: <a href=\"http://causality-and-consequences.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DtD: Causality and Consequence</a><br /> Off-Season: <a href=\"http://lifelong-educations.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">M:tAw- Lifelong Education</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/667-abenniton","name":"ABenniton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar667_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T13:34:29-08:00","id":16765,"title":"","content":"You could play a Wraith rather than trying to force Geist to conform to it. I've seen a couple fanbooks for the nWoD ranging from straight up rules conversions to an actual remake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1021-raneth","name":"Raneth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T14:16:43-08:00","id":16788,"title":"","content":"Wraith the Arising: wraithproject.cattail.nu","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T21:04:09-08:00","id":16923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15982-making-geister-more-important-wraithfying-geist?p=16788#post16788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wraith the Arising: wraithproject.cattail.nu</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think that's the one, or it was on the same site at least. How's that compare to Geist or the classic Wraith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1021-raneth","name":"Raneth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T02:18:06-08:00","id":17037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ABenniton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15982-making-geister-more-important-wraithfying-geist?p=16759#post16759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm curious, even though this is a little bit off topic: What system DO you use to run Geist?</div> </div> </div> </div>I use a Don't Rest Your Head to run pretty much the entire WoD.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T02:18:48-08:00","id":17039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raneth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15982-making-geister-more-important-wraithfying-geist?p=16765#post16765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could play a Wraith rather than trying to force Geist to conform to it. I've seen a couple fanbooks for the nWoD ranging from straight up rules conversions to an actual remake.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I wanted to run Wraith, I'd run Wraith. As you can see in my first post, I think it's fairly evident that I'm going for something different here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T02:31:44-08:00","id":17040,"title":"","content":"We discussed a more wraith-like arrangement for BoS, but elected not to do that as a group.<br /> <br /> It is certainly interesting. I guess my issue is it goes against the dark-yet-upbeat tone of the game somewhat. Geists appear (and it may just be my reading) to be a little more antagonistic in this system, and while I recognize those relationships can exist I am not sure I like it as a default for Geist as written.<br /> <br /> My other note may be totally meaningless to you if your group really likes this idea, but may be important if you are gonna work on it a lot for general consumption. I have found the biggest stumbling block Wraith (and Harrowed in Deadlands) had was players do not like losing control of their characters OOC in a systematic way. My players at least don't mind the character losing control, that can be really interesting (see: Vampire) but what I gather here and elsewhere is that people seem to shy away from that as a major mechanic. <i>Make no mistake, I am not saying don't do this especially if you are primarily doing it for your group, but in terms of what people want to play</i>, that is what I have noticed. Take it for what you will.<br /> <br /> This post came out looking more negative then I intended, I think. Apologies. Your ideas seem sound, just less what I take away from the hopeful message of Geist, I guess. At least, that is my perception of it, I could be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T22:26:33-08:00","id":17519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15982-making-geister-more-important-wraithfying-geist?p=17040#post17040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is certainly interesting. I guess my issue is it goes against the dark-yet-upbeat tone of the game somewhat. Geists appear (and it may just be my reading) to be a little more antagonistic in this system, and while I recognize those relationships can exist I am not sure I like it as a default for Geist as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>My other note may be totally meaningless to you if your group really likes this idea, but may be important if you are gonna work on it a lot for general consumption. I have found the biggest stumbling block Wraith (and Harrowed in Deadlands) had was players do not like losing control of their characters OOC in a systematic way. My players at least don't mind the character losing control, that can be really interesting (see: Vampire) but what I gather here and elsewhere is that people seem to shy away from that as a major mechanic. <i>Make no mistake, I am not saying don't do this especially if you are primarily doing it for your group, but in terms of what people want to play</i>, that is what I have noticed. Take it for what you will.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Valid points. I myself am very fond of the whole struggling not to lose control thing most of the WoD games have going on, and I would like to see it implemented in Geist.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T22:53:15-08:00","id":17525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bigwhitt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15982-making-geister-more-important-wraithfying-geist?p=16181#post16181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why? Why would you ever want to do this? I certainly want to express that I respect you as a player. However, Wraith: The Oblivion was one of the most horrible RPG's that White Wolf ever made...ever. Geist, and the way it works now is a really great system that has become one of my favorite to Storytell in. Bringing more &quot;Wraith&quot; into &quot;Geist&quot; is like saying, &quot;I sure wish there was more Spam in my pumpkin pie! Wouldnt it be great?&quot; No, sir, it would not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiousity, why is that? I've only read a little of Wraith, and never played, so I'm always eager to learn more.<br /> <br /> <b>OP</b>: While of course if playing with the setting and stuff works for you and your group, then go for it, a lot of the reasoning you mention is sort of implicit in Geist to begin with. They <i>are</i> alien, and frequently the things they want <i>are</i> pretty dodgy from a conventional viewpoint. But that's Geist: it's about compromising with the voice in your head that happens to be fused to your very soul and is keeping you alive. Synergy could probably use a bit of revision to represent the relationship between mortal and geist more than obscure laws, but inherently I'd say it works pretty well in that regard.<br /> <br /> Unless of course you just want to fuse it with Wraith because you like Wraith. Then go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T00:02:16-08:00","id":17563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15982-making-geister-more-important-wraithfying-geist?p=17525#post17525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>OP</b>: While of course if playing with the setting and stuff works for you and your group, then go for it, a lot of the reasoning you mention is sort of implicit in Geist to begin with. They <i>are</i> alien, and frequently the things they want <i>are</i> pretty dodgy from a conventional viewpoint. But that's Geist: it's about compromising with the voice in your head that happens to be fused to your very soul and is keeping you alive. Synergy could probably use a bit of revision to represent the relationship between mortal and geist more than obscure laws, but inherently I'd say it works pretty well in that regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's there, yes, but not as pronounced as I would like it. I want systems for bargaining with the Geist for more power in exchange for doing things the Geist wants to happen. I also want systems for the Geist to try and take over the body if pushed to do so.<br /> <br /> You could say that I would like to emphasize these things a little more. I tend to mess with the settings and systems of these games a lot, so it's not so much a criticism of the official game, which is golden, instead of me customizing the game to make it more suitable for the purposes of my group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T03:00:59-08:00","id":17631,"title":"","content":"What about using the GMC system of ambition, letting a couple of them (or three new ones!) be defined by the geister?<br /> In this way, there would be no &quot;conflict&quot;, but &quot;compromise&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you wish to make thing a little bit harder for the bounds, make Keys / psyche / manifestations only buyable with such experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1304-baroqo","name":"Baroqo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T07:54:48-08:00","id":22335,"title":"","content":"Do you have Danse Macabre for Vampire? It seems to me that the atrocity dice system might be worth employing here - instead of hurting people, add dice for following the agenda of the geist - maybe the questions could be &quot;did you <i>take its suggestion</i> to follow its agenda,&quot; &quot;do you fear you might have failed if not for following its agenda,&quot; and &quot;did its agenda feel good,&quot; with a die added for each yes, and one subtracted if you can answer yes to &quot;can I justify it (in terms of something that <i>isn't</i> its agenda),&quot; resulting in 0-3 dice added for doing what the geist wants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T11:14:40-08:00","id":28117,"title":"","content":"This is in response to the overall thread content and not any particular post within it.<br /> <br /> I think a good alternate solution would be if Wraiths represented ghosts that simply can't go to the Underworld. With Vampires and Mummies we have examples of Undead creatures. Wraiths should represent dead things that are deeply bound to the mortal world. They are so deeply bound that they've are disconnected from the Underworld and other types of spirits. The old Wraith system's powers actually made this possible but, the Underworld setting was so well developed that there was no reason to ever set an adventure in the &quot;real world.&quot; Any new version of Wraith would need to address this, as all of nWoD games are set up around interactions with people. <br /> <br /> Two good mechanics to bring into Wraith are Changeling's seemings, which I envision could be used to define the kind of dead thing masquerading as a human and Promethean's Disquiet/Wasteland mechanic. Wasteland size would need to be toned down some (it needs this in Promethean too).<br /> <br /> I think also a slightly different central theme would be helpful. Instead of resolving one's unfinished business a more helpful theme would be overcoming death. Instead of overcoming fear of the unknown it becomes achieve despite the obstacles. The core thing that every Wraith wants to do is to live again. They are literally restless dead.<br /> <br /> Since they are cut off from the Underworld a Vampire-esque feed off of life mechanic could also be added.<br /> <br /> Just my 2 pence worth anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T12:43:29-08:00","id":28213,"title":"","content":"Jacob, this isn't intended as criticism, but does your post have anything to do with my original post?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T12:16:05-08:00","id":28871,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's an alternate view. Rather than &quot;wraithify&quot; geists, one could just build a new Wraith game. IMO, there is room for both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T02:55:15-08:00","id":29217,"title":"","content":"That could be an interesting thread, but in this thread lets stick to the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}